reviewCommentsList.body:
Consider adding a lambda to reduce duplicate code:
>        auto update = [&](auto const& sField) {
>              if (auto const field = ctx_.tx[~sField])
>              {
>                  if (field->empty())
>                  {
>                      sleDID->makeFieldAbsent(sField);
>                  }
>                  else
>                  {
>                      (*sleDID)[sField] = *field;
>                  }
>              }
>        };
>        update(sfURI);
>        update(sfDIDDocument);
>        update(sfAttestation);

Consider adding lambda:
>       auto set = [&](auto const& sField) {
>        if (auto const field = ctx_.tx[~sField];
>           field.has_value() && !field->empty())
>            (*sleDID)[sField] = field.value();
>      };
>      set(sfURI);
>      set(sfDIDDocument);
>      set(sfAttestation);

Consider simplifying. Don't really need these variables.
>         if (!ctx.view.read(keylet::did(ctx.tx[sfAccount])) &&
>            !ctx.tx.isFieldPresent(sfURI) && !ctx.tx.isFieldPresent(sfDIDDocument))
>            return tecEMPTY_DID;
>
>         return tesSUCCESS;

Consider this:
>     auto malformed = [&](auto const& sField, std::size_t length) -> bool {
>         if (auto field = ctx.tx[~sField])
>             return field->length() > length;
>         return false;
>     };
>     if (malformed(sfURI, maxDIDURILength) ||
>         malformed(sfDIDDocument, maxDIDDocumentLength) ||
>         malformed(sfAttestation, maxDIDAttestationLength))
>         return temMALFORMED;

We tend not to use `has_value` and `value` . Consider rewriting this in a similar style to your `update` lambda above. I.e. something like:
```
        if (auto const field = ctx_.tx[~sField]; field && !field->empty())
            (*sleDID)[sField] = *field;
```
